# Netlify-specific redirects file. Read by Netlify at deploy time;
# AWS S3+CloudFront ignores it (will sit as a plain text file at
# /_redirects on the AWS-served site, which is harmless).
#
# Why we need this: Netlify Identity's invite emails generate links of
# the form https://<netlify-subdomain>/?invite_token=... pointing at the
# site root. We host the Decap CMS UI at /admin/, so we rewrite root to
# the admin index page. The invite_token query string is preserved, the
# Identity widget on the admin page detects it, and the signup flow
# kicks off normally.
#
# Status 200 = rewrite (URL stays /), as opposed to 301/302 (redirect).
# Rewrite is the right call so Netlify Identity sees the token in the
# URL the widget actually loads from.

/  /admin/index.html  200
